The eccentricity of the ellipse $y^{2}+4 x^{2}-12 x+6 y+14=0$ is $\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}$.
Given ellipse,
$\begin{array}{l}
y^{2}+4 x^{2}-12 x+6 y+14=0 \\
4 x^{2}-12 x+y^{2}+6 y+14=0 \\
4\left(x^{2}-3 x+\frac{9}{4}\right)+y^{2}+6 y+9=-14+9+9 \\
4\left(x-\frac{3}{2}\right)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4 \\
\frac{\left(x-\frac{3}{2}\right)^{2}}{1}+\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4}=1
\end{array}
Here, $ a^{2}=1, $ b^{2}=4\begin{array}{l}
\therefore$ e=$\sqrt{1-\frac{a^{2}}{b^{2}}}$\\
e=$\sqrt{1-\frac{1}{4}}
\end{array}$

